## 2026-08-23 (cont.)
- Slices 1 (FE catalog) and 2 (BE chat intake) both completed and PR'd (#5, #4). The process crashed mid-run and restarted; both agents had already committed and pushed before that happened, so no work was lost, but the recovery surfaced a real operational gap: this session dispatches subagents into the *same* working directory rather than isolated worktrees, and two agents doing `git checkout -b`/commit concurrently nearly collided (FE's uncommitted work got rescued via a targeted `git stash push --keep-index -- frontend/` mid-race). Worth using `isolation: "worktree"` for any future parallel agent dispatch instead.
- Somewhere in the crash/restart, PR #4 and #5 got merged without INT ever completing a verification pass — the responsible process is unclear (possibly a pre-crash INT agent still running, possibly leftover from an earlier turn). Not reverted since the code was sound, but it's exactly the gap INT was supposed to close, and it bit us: see next line.
- User added a real `GEMINI_API_KEY` to `backend/.env`. Live-tested `/chat/intake` for the first time and found two real bugs the mocked unit tests couldn't catch: (1) `response_schema` as a `types.Schema` instance crashes this SDK version — must be a plain dict; (2) `gemini-2.0-flash-lite` is retired, API pointed at `gemini-3.5-flash-lite`. Fixed both, verified live call + tests both pass, PR #6 opened.
- Separately: `gh pr merge` is blocked by Claude Code's own auto-mode safety classifier (harness-level, not a CLAUDE.md setting) — PRs can be opened but not merged from here. #6 needs a manual merge.
- Self-inflicted near-miss: ran `git checkout main && git reset --hard origin/main` while my own uncommitted fix was sitting in the working tree, wiping it. Recovered by reapplying the same two-line fix from memory since I'd just written and verified it, but the lesson is to check `git status`/stash before any `reset --hard`, full stop.

